 succeeded in 503ms:
{"body":"## Summary\n\n- Fixed bug where 'No onPostToolUseHook found' messages leaked past noise suppression\n- Changed approach from skip-entire-chunk to strip-patterns-from-content\n- Handles both standalone noise and embedded noise concatenated with real content\n\n## Details\n\nThe hook warning messages were leaking into ralph output because they were concatenated directly with agent messages (no newline separator). The previous suppression logic checked if the entire chunk matched a noise pattern and skipped it, but this failed when noise was embedded within real content like:\n\n```\nExcellent creative brief. Now launching Phase 2...No onPostToolUseHook found for tool use ID: toolu_01LCkxN6GwoWUfvy7wqwp3sW\n```\n\n## Changes\n\n- Renamed `SUPPRESSED_PATTERNS` to `NOISE_PATTERNS` with more precise regex\n- Replaced `shouldSuppress()` with `stripNoise()` that removes patterns from content\n- `stripNoise` returns cleaned content or null if entirely noise\n- Preserves whitespace for proper streaming accumulation\n- Added tests for embedded noise stripping and multi-pattern handling\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Standalone noise messages still suppressed\n- [x] Embedded noise is stripped while preserving surrounding content\n- [x] Multiple noise patterns in same chunk are all stripped\n- [x] Content accumulation across chunks works correctly\n- [x] Works for both agent_message_chunk and agent_thought_chunk\n\nTask: @01KGVAZ6\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":[{"path":"src/ralph/events.ts","additions":37,"deletions":21},{"path":"tests/ralph.test.ts","additions":57,"deletions":2}],"title":"fix(ralph): strip noise patterns instead of skipping entire chunks"}

